| `make trace` `[local]` | Judges every requirement a `kind: spec` document defines as `covered` (a collected test names it with the `req` marker), `gap` (a config row excuses it with a reason) or `uncovered`, and writes the matrix. It is a `make verify` goal. | `make trace` | [`traceability.specs_root`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`traceability.gaps`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`traceability.matrix_path`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Says a test names a requirement, not that the test proves it: it imports no test. Refuses (exit 2) a symlinked path, a matrix path git does not ignore or the filesystem will not write, and a document under the specs root that defines a requirement without `kind: spec`. Its verdict counts are not in the evidence record: only pytest's are. | [dev-loops.md](../guides/dev-loops.md) | always |
